AVAR Kantar — Third-Party Software Licenses
============================================

This folder contains the full, unmodified license texts of the
open-source components shipped with AVAR Kantar. All rights of the
respective components belong to their original authors.

The application itself (AVAR Kantar) is proprietary; the licenses
below apply ONLY to the specific third-party components listed.

Components and their licenses
-----------------------------

  * Qt for Python (PySide6, shiboken6) — LGPLv3
      -> LGPL-3.0.txt (and GPL-3.0.txt, referenced by the LGPL)
      Qt is used dynamically via separate DLLs shipped alongside the
      program (folder: AVAR Kantar/PySide6/*). These DLLs may be
      replaced by the end user with LGPL-compatible builds obtained
      from the Qt Project. AVAR Kantar has NOT modified Qt.
      Qt itself contains further third-party components; see
      https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/licenses-used-in-qt.html

  * FFmpeg (bundled with Qt Multimedia, IP-camera playback) — LGPL v2.1+
      -> ffmpeg-NOTICE.txt (version, build configuration, source)
      -> LGPL-2.1.txt, ffmpeg-LICENSE.md
      Separate, replaceable DLLs (avcodec/avformat/avutil/swresample/
      swscale) in the program folder. AVAR Kantar has NOT modified FFmpeg.

  * Python — PSF License 2.0
      -> PSF-2.0.txt, python-LICENSE.txt (the license file of the exact
         Windows build shipped, including the terms for the Microsoft
         Visual C++ runtime files vcruntime140*.dll / msvcp140*.dll)
      Bundled with Python: expat (MIT) -> expat-COPYING.txt,
                           libffi (MIT) -> libffi-LICENSE.txt

  * SQLCipher (community edition) — 3-clause BSD
      -> sqlcipher-LICENSE.txt
      Python binding sqlcipher3 — MIT -> sqlcipher3-LICENSE.txt

  * cryptography — Apache 2.0 OR 3-clause BSD (dual licensed)
      -> cryptography-LICENSE.txt, cryptography-LICENSE.APACHE.txt,
         cryptography-LICENSE.BSD.txt
      cffi (used by cryptography) — MIT -> cffi-LICENSE.txt

  * OpenSSL (bundled with Python and cryptography) — Apache 2.0
      -> openssl-LICENSE.txt / Apache-2.0.txt

  * openpyxl — MIT
      -> openpyxl-LICENSE.txt
      et_xmlfile (used by openpyxl) — MIT
      -> et_xmlfile-LICENCE.txt, et_xmlfile-LICENCE-python.txt

  * defusedxml — PSF License
      -> defusedxml-LICENSE.txt

  * xlrd — BSD
      -> xlrd-LICENSE.txt

  * pyserial — 3-clause BSD
      -> pyserial-LICENSE.txt

  * pywin32 — PSF-derived BSD
      -> pywin32-LICENSE.txt

  * Lucide Icons — ISC (with historical MIT contributions)
      -> lucide-LICENSE.txt

  * Further components (NumPy, OpenCV, ONNX Runtime and others) —
    MIT / Apache 2.0 / BSD / MPL-2.0
      -> components-LICENSES.txt (every component, version and full text)

Where to obtain sources
-----------------------

Sources for every LGPL / GPL-covered component are available from
the upstream project pages, e.g.:
  * Qt / PySide6  — https://www.qt.io/  |  https://pypi.org/project/PySide6/
  * FFmpeg        — see ffmpeg-NOTICE.txt
  * Python        — https://www.python.org/
  * OpenSSL       — https://www.openssl.org/
  * SQLCipher     — https://www.zetetic.net/sqlcipher/
